{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Issue a formal apology for the UK\u2019s role in the 1943 Bengal Famine",
        "additional_details": "During WWII, the UK Government enacted a \u201cDenial Policy\u201d in Bengal, confiscating or destroying food stocks and destroying transport boats which crippled the economy. As starvation spread, requests for emergency food imports were repeatedly denied by London.\r\n \r\nWhile the UK Government has expressed regret for some events like Jallianwala Bagh, it has never formally apologised for the UK Government\u2019s administrative choices that allowed millions of colonial subjects to perish from preventable hunger.",
        "background": "We call on the UK Government to issue a formal apology to India, Bangladesh and Pakistan for policies enacted by the British War Cabinet, which we feel caused or severely worsened the 1943 Bengal Famine and was estimated to have led to 3 million deaths.",
